        "original_id": "ac06a8ca-a456-5c28-bcba-c9329eed30ff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: St Mary's Chapel, Rattray; Castle of Rattray; Scotland\n- People: William Comyn\n- Roles: jure uxoris Earl of Buchan\n- Concepts: private chapel; dedication to the Virgin Mary\n\nFacts:\n- The Castle of Rattray was a medieval Scottish castle that underwent multiple structural variations over approximately six centuries.\n- William Comyn, jure uxoris Earl of Buchan, built St Mary's Chapel, Rattray during the same period as the Castle of Rattray.\n- St Mary's Chapel, Rattray served as a private chapel for the Castle of Rattray and its residents.\n- St Mary's Chapel, Rattray was dedicated to the Virgin Mary.\n- St Mary's Chapel, Rattray may have been constructed after the drowning of a son of William Comyn in a nearby well.",
